This package bundles third-party icon data and fonts under `sets/`.
The package's own source code is MIT licensed; see LICENSE.

================================================================================
sets/file-icons/
================================================================================

`icondb.js` and the source Less files under `tools/` are taken from the
file-icons package for Atom:

    https://github.com/file-icons/atom
    Copyright (c) 2014-2016 Daniel Brooker
    Copyright (c) 2016-2025 John Gardner
    MIT License

The fonts it references come from four separate projects:

  file-icons.woff2   https://github.com/file-icons/icons
                     ISC License

  mfixx.woff2        https://github.com/file-icons/MFixx
                     MIT License
                     A fork of Font-Mfizz by Matt Ball.

  devopicons.woff2   https://github.com/file-icons/DevOpicons
                     Derived from Devicons by Theodore Vorillas
                     (https://github.com/vorillaz/devicons), MIT License.
                     NOTE: the DevOpicons fork itself carries no LICENSE file.

  fontawesome.woff2  Font Awesome 4.7.0 by Dave Gandy
                     https://fontawesome.com
                     SIL OFL 1.1 (font), MIT License (CSS)

Twenty entries in the icon table point at "Octicons Regular", the editor's own
bundled UI font. No Octicons font file is redistributed here.

================================================================================
sets/seti/
================================================================================

`vs-seti-icon-theme.json` and `seti.woff` are taken from the theme-seti
extension bundled with Visual Studio Code:

    https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/tree/main/extensions/theme-seti
    Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation
    MIT License

The manifest is generated from the Seti UI theme by Jesse Weed:

    https://github.com/jesseweed/seti-ui
    Copyright (c) 2014 Jesse Weed
    MIT License

The `information_for_contributors` block inside the manifest is preserved
verbatim; upstream fixes belong in jesseweed/seti-ui.
